ect, and I was tasked with building an accessible data visualization web tool up from scratch. This was a major challenge for me since I had no prior experience setting up a Node.js environment, a server with Express, or a postgreSQL database, all of which were things I needed to learn. While the project is still in progress, (I am currently redesigning the frontend to use React) I was able to create an effective prototype that handles the data management, and I am very proud of my work so far.	GitHub: https://github.com/owennjpr, FreeBites: https://github.com/freebites/product 	3	6	4	5	10	11	8	9	1	2	7	12	English at Large sounds like an exciting project to me and is my top choice because it has a clear and important audience, and creating a cataloguing system for their resources sounds like a fun and interesting challenge. Bread & Roses sounds like a great organization, and food insecurity is a deeply important issue. Creating a volunteer management system sounds like a great way to positively impact their ability to do important work. The West Medford Community Center project also sounds very interesting to me, since I think community centers are super useful and important, and being able to effectively market them with a newsletter is critical.	\N	I have not	Otho Sackville-Baggins	
