	she/her	2027	Yes	I’m excited to join JumboCode because it offers the perfect blend of community engagement and technical growth. Being part of a group that’s focused on using technology for social good deeply resonates with my passion for making a tangible impact. I’m eager to connect with like-minded individuals who are equally driven to create solutions that benefit others, and I see JumboCode as a place where I can contribute to projects that truly make a difference.\nI’m particularly interested in web development and full-stack development, and I’m looking forward to applying my current skills to meaningful causes that help real people. At the same time, I’m excited to expand my knowledge, learn from the talented peers around me, and work on projects that challenge me to grow. For me, JumboCode isn’t just about coding—it's about collaboration, making lasting contributions, and growing together as a team.	I have a diverse range of experience in volunteering, community engagement, and working with non-profits. I volunteered with Knowsnack, a startup focused on creating digital flashcards for children, where I collaborated with a team to redesign their website and integrate a payment gateway. I also developed a WhatsApp chatbot for managing flashcard attributes and conducted user and competitor research to guide design decisions. My role involved creating pseudocode for front-end implementation using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Additionally, as a Teaching Assistant at Tufts University, I assisted in C++ data structures labs, graded assignments, and provided weekly office hours to support students in debugging their code. I also volunteered as a video editor and graphics producer for my local TV station, where I worked with non-profit organizations to create videos and support their causes. 	Yes	Yes	Mondays after 5, Tuesdays 2-4:30, Wednesdays after 5, Fridays after 6, all of Saturdays	CS 11: Intro to Computer Science, CS 15: Data Structures, Web Art	C/C++, HTML/CSS, JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Git/GitHub, Python	My first introduction to computer science was through my senior thesis project, where I built a pixel platformer game using Java. This project was a unique opportunity to incorporate Filipino culture into the gaming space. I spearheaded the development of core game mechanics, such as monster AI, movement, attacks, and tile implementation. I also faced and overcame several challenges, including optimizing game performance and balancing gameplay elements to create an engaging experience.	One project that really excited me was an interactive art installation I developed called By The Car Window. The goal of the project was to create an immersive experience where users could interact with a digital environment through hand gestures. I led the entire development process, utilizing TouchDesigner, Python, and UltraLeap technology to bring it to life.\n\nThe core of the installation involved using Leap Motion sensors to track users' hand movements. I designed a motion-tracking system that captured these gestures in real-time, allowing users to interact with an illustrated car window environment. As users moved their hands, they could manipulate objects outside the car window—such as changing the weather or adjusting the landscape—creating a dynamic, personalized experience.\n\nOne of the major challenges was ensuring precise hand-tracking and smooth interaction. Leap Motion sensors can be sensitive, and I had to fine-tune the system to avoid lag and ensure that every gesture translated accurately on the screen. Additionally, I had to balance the aesthetic aspects with the technical demands, making sure that the visuals and interactions felt natural and engaging while maintaining performance.\n\nUltimately, this project was a rewarding challenge because it merged art, technology, and interaction in a way that captivated users and pushed me to refine my skills in both creative coding and interactive design.	https://github.com/acabochan	12	8	7	5	10	2	1	11	3	6	4	9	The LGBTQ Senior Housing project resonates with me because it addresses the unique economic and social challenges faced by LGBTQ seniors, many of whom have led the fight for LGBTQ rights. The progress made—whether legalizing same-sex marriage or securing workplace protections—rests on the shoulders of these elders. I feel a responsibility to honor their contributions by ensuring they have access to safe, affordable housing. LGBTQ seniors often face discrimination, isolation, and lack of family support, making welcoming and inclusive housing vital. What excites me about this project isn't just about providing housing but also creating a space for connection and community building.\n\nThe New England Innocence Project (NEIP) also stands out. Their work in correcting wrongful convictions addresses systemic issues in the criminal justice system that disproportionately affects marginalized groups. Wrongful arrests often stem from racial bias, socioeconomic inequality, and inadequate legal representation. NEIP’s work to exonerate individuals requires immense data, coordination, and time. I believe technology has the power to be a step in solving these social issues, and building an exoneree database that streamlines client management for the NEIP could make a huge difference in their advocacy work.\n\nThe English at Large project draws me in due to its focus on helping immigrants improve their English skills. As someone from a Filipino immigrant household, I’ve seen how challenging it can be to learn a second language, especially when it’s essential for navigating everyday life, from securing employment to simply feeling a sense of belonging in a new country. My family’s experience has shown me how language barriers can create feelings of isolation. That’s why I’m passionate about initiatives like this, which aim to reduce those barriers and open up new opportunities for immigrants. Helping to build a system that supports this mission resonates with me on a personal level.\n\nOverall I would be extremely appreciative to join any of these initiatives or projects. I am deeply passionate about social work and hope to be a part of supporting a community in any way I can. I would be extremely appreciative to join any project and hope I can contribute my skills effectively. 	\N	\N	Fili	
