 anytime before 3 and after 5, and basically every weekday after 7:15!	CS 11: Intro to Computer Science	C/C++, HTML/CSS, JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Git/GitHub, Python	13! (High School Freshman Year) – Intro to CS (Java + Python)!	During my senior year of high school, to graduate from my “major”, I had to take CS Capstone, a full year class dedicated to creating a product for a client. In groups of three to five, we were required to go through the process of product development, starting with contacting clients, producing a minimum viable product, and finally presenting our product in front of a panel of experts in the industry.\n\nAfter reaching out to multiple clients, my group ultimately worked with JoAh Academy, a newly founded test prep academy that provided 5-12th grade extra-curricular learning services and college consulting. Our client was looking for a way to digitize their processes as they fully operated on paper, including grading and testing. They asked us to focus on three main tasks – a new home website to act as a central hub for their clients, a testing environment to simulate digital standardized exams, and facilitated communication between students and teachers. By the end of the year, my group had created a home website as well as a dashboard system for students and teachers. Teachers/Admin would be able to create short quizzes as well as longer PDF exams, send announcements to students, administer new students, and read inquiries sent from the main website. Students would be able to read announcements and take short quizzes or PDF exams. Our tech stack involved Django, SQLite, Bootstrap, and GitHub.\n\nBecause this was our group's first time building a large scale project and working heavily with web development, we struggled a lot with time management, directory organization, and even choosing a tech stack. Setting realistic expectations and presenting problems to our non tech-savvy client proved to be difficult as well. Another big challenge was working with databases and learning about security, including penetration testing! Through all these problems, with trial and error, teamwork, and time, we were able to get through all these challenges and produce a super cool project.	Capstone Project MVP: https://joahtestprep.pythonanywhere.com/	4	5	9	7	2	11	8	3	10	1	6	12	Bread & Roses is my top choice because throughout high school, I used to volunteer at my local church’s program for elderly individuals facing food insecurity and would love to continue making a positive impact within my college community. Additionally, I am interested in working on a web application that can streamline manual processes, particularly through new communication and scheduling features, as I have worked on similar projects in the past! My second choice was Dillar Academy because I am an English tutor for underprivileged kids living in Korea. For my high school senior project, I made a program where teachers could enroll students and share material with them! For similar reasons, I placed LCS Tutoring high on my ranking due to their educational initiatives. Overall, I am excited about all the projects as they all equally offer an opportunity to help or provide support for our surrounding communities while learning new software and technologies.	\N	Yes, I was a part of Sibling Connections last year!	Amdir	
