ct of the project that was challenging was that we all had no prior experience with React, so we were learning it as we were building out this product. I had to become comfortable with being uncomfortable and rely on my teammates just as they relied on me. We all had different strengths and were really able to come together in order to create the page, with a bunch of additional features, that we were proud to show to our boss and the company executives. 	\N	6	7	12	4	8	11	10	9	3	5	2	1	The Tufts University Counsel Project really stuck out to me as a first choice. Despite being last to present at the GIM, they really broadcasted a passion for what they were working on and drew me in. This project interests me because it is directly helping those who use medical services, which means they are having a large outreach. Being able to check the reliability of a medical professional is something that is so important, and it is so cool that their project is going to help with that. In addition, I've had experience this past summer coding in ReactJS at my internship and would love to contribute! I'd also love to work in Python. A2 Empowerment was my second choice and also excited me during the GIM. I think the purpose of the project is so powerful, and helping women gain access to education has a true impact. 	\N	No I have not	Eöl	
