ear of high school.	A project I am particularly proud of was during my role as a Student Office Assistant at the Tufts Math Department. I was tasked with creating an automated process using Microsoft Power Automate to replace the department's physical TA contracts, which were prone to getting misplaced.\nAlthough I had no prior experience with Power Automate, I was determined to learn the platform using any available resources. I began by familiarizing myself with the Power Automate interface, exploring several templates to understand its uses. Once I felt more comfortable, I mapped out the workflow.\nThe process I designed was triggered by form submissions, which were then routed to the relevant instructors for approval. I added a step that generated a .pdf file with the form information, allowing instructors to review it. Upon approval, email notifications were automatically sent to all involved parties. I also implemented an extra feature where the data from the form submissions was entered into an Excel spreadsheet, creating a centralized and easily accessible database for the department.\nDespite facing challenges, like integrating OneDrive and Excel, I used online resources, including YouTube tutorials and forum discussions to resolve them. This project not only improved the department’s efficiency, but also provided me with a satisfying learning experience in with a real impact on the department’s operations.	\N	11	6	8	12	3	7	10	2	5	1	4	9	As a passion-driven person, I am most motivated by causes that resonate with me, like those focused on promoting equity, education, and access to essential resources.\nOne issue deeply concerns me is food insecurity. I believe no one should face the inability to access a basic necessity like food. Considering the number of people affected by this issue, I would love to  I would love to contribute to a project like Bread & Roses, where I could help optimize efficiency and impact.\n\nEducation is one of my core values, as show