/reddit-politics-sentiment-analysis#updates	12	8	6	1	10	11	9	2	3	5	4	7	Out of all the projects listed above, I'm especially attracted by the Somerville Museum project. Before I entered the field of CS, I have been practicing and enjoying Fine Arts and Art History ever since I was small. I've done researches on numerous artists and art periods and have a very solid understanding of the historical development of art. I'm also intrigued by the chance to design an efficient user interface and data organization, using my distinguished understanding of the art pieces. \nMoreover, I've put a few tutoring projects as my next few preferences, as I've been tutoring students ever since high school until now and deeply acknowledges my interest and engagement in providing help to those who are in need. It is especially meaningful for me to contribute to the educational projects listed above. 	\N	Yes! I've attended JumboHack before and developed a project called Reddit Political Sentiment Analysis, which got an Honorable Mention award. 	Durin's Bane	
