ce, I enjoyed being thrown into the realm of robotics research.	Last semester, I went to Hack@Brown where I created a concept of a website that essentially matched devs to people who have project ideas. We split the work into two parts: front end and back end. In the front end, we hosted our website locally and used HTML, CSS, and Javascript. For the backend, we utilized an algorithm similar to online dating apps, and searched for keywords. The algorithm updated with user input (clicking a button for yes/no)\nOur entire website was essentially a dating app for devs and project leaders, and it was meant to bring ideas to life. 	\N	7	5	4	6	11	10	9	1	2	3	12	8	I'm really interested in supporting women in all aspects in life. I'm currently the Social Chair for Women in CS and Logistics chair for Women in Tech, which is why bringing educational opportunities to women in Cameroon spoke to me. Additionally, I saw that AWS would be used in the tech stack, and I am looking into cloud computing! 	Eager and ready to join!	\N	Brodda	
