s time to apply the new designs, where I struggled with finding the balance of making changes to the application to fit the design vs adjusting the design to align with the structure of the code. Through this process I was able to learn a lot about the development and design processes. 	\N	3	1	8	12	10	4	6	2	11	9	7	5	I chose my preferences based on the missions of the projects. I'm particularly interested in initiatives that directly impact the Medford/Somerville community. Additionally, I would find it especially rewarding to work on projects involving Tufts groups, as it is possible I would be impacting people that I know. I am excited for the opportunity to learn any new technologies so I didn't base my decisions too much on the tech stack.	\N	\N	Baragund	
