 I'm available on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays after about 4:15pm. My availability is open for Fridays and Saturdays as well! (And of course for the Sunday meetings).	CS 11: Intro to Computer Science	C/C++, HTML/CSS, JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Git/GitHub	My first introduction to CS was an Introduction to Programming class in my sophomore year of high school. The class was taught in basic Python, and I loved seeing my code turn into visualizations of Christmas trees and other drawings on my screen!	A project I’m proud of is my personal website that I built on Replit during a Girls Who Code summer program. The personal website has multiple sub-sites linked within to lead to sections such as About Me (which includes a button-activated random fact generator), a gallery of photos I’ve taken, and a tab for my current projects/interests. I built the website by planning the content, putting it into HTML, making the different sub-sites, formatting the sizing, coloring, spacing, fonts, and overall style in CSS, and creating my fact generator in JavaScript. I faced challenges specifically with both learning how to use and understanding Flexbox, which produced the most bugs in my code; I had to give up some Flexbox features after 4 hours straight, but I figured out a workaround that still allowed for the basic margins/spacing I was looking for. I’ve linked this website below, but it might now work because I don’t pay for Replit; I hope it does though, because I’m really proud of how it turned out!	Since I can't publish the website, here is a public edit link so you can have access to everything and launch the website from here! : https://replit.com/join/rueapoevgw-ksdeane 	2	1	5	12	6	3	10	4	7	11	8	9	1. Village Food Hub is my first choice because I’m really drawn to both the team leads and the fact that the project seeks to help a food pantry! As a woman in tech myself, I would absolutely love the opportunity to work with an all-female group of team leads and learn more