activism and sustainability was actually being able to work with my highschool administration to implement a compost program and to get renewable energy sources on campus like solar panels. Also, I am a TA for CS11!	Yes	Yes	Monday: 10:00 am - 1:00 pm or 7:30 pm to 10:00 pm\nTuesday: 9:00 pm - 10:00 pm\nThursday: 5:00 pm - 8:00 pm\nFriday: 1:00 pm - 6:00 pm\nSaturday: Generally in the afternoon or early evening	CS 11: Intro to Computer Science	C/C++, Python	I did an internship in a USC chemical engineering and materials science lab. It was entirely computational so I had to learn python	For my high school senior project, I worked with a non-profit organization that focused on providing clothing and hygiene items to underserved communities in the area to redesign their ordering system to stock their hygiene kit making station. When I started, there was no information about what items were most desired or how many of each item were being distributed each month. I started by creating an online form for volunteers to track item distribution amounts. I did face some challenges with having volunteers consistently and accurately complete the form. So, I started taking inventory of all the in stock items during my shifts and then estimating the daily distribution based on these numbers instead. I then compared these results to the survey to confirm overall accuracy. I also created and carried out a survey that asked people about their most desired items. I compiled all this data collected over a month into a spreadsheet and determined which items were most essential. I also performed an analysis of the cost to try to minimize any unnecessary expenses. This was also difficult because some of the preferred items were expensive. For example, many people preferred the travel size secret deodorant that was occasionally offered instead of the cheaper non name brand travel size deodorant. I put an emphasis on trying to offer nicer products when they were in high demand and less nice products that were in low demand. At the end of a month period, I proposed a monthly ordering plan that was approved by the organization, and then I put all of the items on auto order so the hygiene station would always be stocked. 	\N	7	1	10	8	9	3	11	6	4	2	5	12	I ranked Village Hub Food and Bread and Roses as my top two preferences because the projects align most strongly with the type of volunteer and community service work I most enjoy doing. As I mentioned previously in my application, I care a lot about the issue of homelessness and I think that food and housing insecurity go hand in hand. I would love the opportunity to work on either of these projects and to make even the smallest difference on this front. I am also extremely interested in the New England Innocence project as well. I think injustice in our legal system is a huge problem, so I would enjoy contributing to a project that could help change this. Even though I am most interested in my top three choices, I would still love to work on any of the projects.	\N	No	Ulfang	
