	she/her/hers	2028	Yes	JumboCode offers me an opportunity to combine my love for service alongside my love for creating programs. Becoming a member of JumboCode allows me to broaden my skills involving programming through creating products geared more towards clients rather than simply solving an issue that's presented.	Throughout my time in high school, I've participated in various volunteering organizations (Key Club, Science National Honor Society, Chinese Class TA, etc.) and have also created software applications that worked to solve issues that I cared about. One particular project was an app using MIT app inventor (a block-based programming language) to create an app that included more access to basic needs and resources for low-income and immigrants within our city.	Yes	Yes	I'm available most weekdays after 3PM except for Wednesdays. My weekends are completely free as well.	CS 11: Intro to Computer Science, AP CSA; Data Structures, Advanced Java	C/C++, HTML/CSS, Python	My first introduction to computer science was through the MIT Beaver Works online course where I learned the basics of python. Soon after, I took on my school's AP CSA curriculum, where I learned the basics of programming in Java.	During the summer before my senior year, I attended a program under Northeastern University where I learned to storyboard, design, and program a virtual reality game using C# on the Unity engine. Due to the short time constraint (two weeks) and the lack of knowledge each of our team members, including myself, had on the C# language and the Unity engine, it was difficult to fulfill all the goals my teammates and I originally had in mind, yet we managed to create a virtual reality game that was somewhat playable in the end. What made the experience stand out was that I'd never truly created a program where I had to really evaluate who the audience is and how I should cater to said audience, yet it was insightful to be able to add that part to the brainstorming process.