p provides real-time exchange rates between two currencies, displays a one-month historic rate graph, and even evaluates whether the current rate is favorable. Our goal was to build something practical that could help people make more informed decisions about when to exchange currencies (which was inspired by my struggle with reloading Flywire everyday to figure out the best exchange rate to pay my tuition).\n\nWe built the app using a prediction algorithm powered by a Python-based backend and Shiny’s GUI system to keep the interface simple and intuitive. I worked on the web-based components using Web Assembly, which was a challenge but ultimately improved the app’s speed and performance. One of the biggest technical hurdles we faced was scraping the currency data efficiently, and me and my team solved this by using regular expressions to handle large sets of data. Throughout the process, we used GitHub for version control to manage updates and keep everything organized, and we successfully deployed the app as a fully interactive website.\n\nWhat made this project exciting for me was not only solving technical challenges but also seeing how the app could be useful in the real world. It ended up winning three awards at the hackathon, including “Most Readily Employable” and “Best Financial Hack” with Capital One, which was really rewarding after all the hard work we put in.	Linkedin: www.linkedin.com/in/leann-dinh	5	10	2	4	9	1	12	6	7	11	3	8	I’m particularly drawn to projects that have a real, positive impact on people’s lives. My top choices are all aligned with that focus, whether it’s working to bring justice to those wrongfully convicted, supporting students navigating challenges without a safety net, or empowering women through education.\n\nWhat I find exciting about these kinds of projects is the opportunity to make processes more efficient and help organizations achieve their missions more effectively. I want to contribute to work that not only uses my technical skills but also makes a tangible difference in people’s lives. Each of these projects offers a chance to do just that, and that’s what motivates me.	None.	I have not been a part of Jumbocode.	Thrain	
