, and errors we have never heard of before which were especially frustrating as there are no office hours for club projects. After countless hours, we eventually got the correct temp and humidity to be displayed in the terminal, now how do we display that in the greenhouse? We scoured through Nolop to find a lcd display (that we were allowed to use) and had to figure out the correct wiring to display what the terminal was outputting onto the display. I have minimal experience working with wires so it was a lot of fun learning about circuits hands on. By the grand opening of the greenhouse we got the sensor up and working for everyone to view!\n\nI am very proud of this project as it was my first time working on a programming related project outside of school and the fact that it will be playing a part in teaching sustainability to others excited me even more! \n	\N	2	3	9	11	10	7	4	1	5	8	6	12	I chose LCS tutoring as my first choice because of my experience being tutored for the SAT. I have never been a great test taker so when it came to standardized tests I always had trouble focusing and finishing. After seeing my first scores, my parents and I decided it was best that I got a tutor. By the first session I already felt more confident in my abilities as my tutor taught me a more streamlined and strategic approach as opposed to my previous brute force approach. Because of tutoring I was able to increase my score from below average to Tufts University level! Because of this experience I have the utmost respect for tutoring and would be ecstatic to have the opportunity to play a part in developing a web app that can perfectly match tutors and tutees’ so that more students can reap the same benefits of tutoring as I did.\n\nI chose West Medford Community Center as my second choice because I believe that connecting with others with diverse backgrounds is one of life’s greatest pleasures. Coming from a majority white area, Tufts has presented me with the opportunity to meet and befriend so many people with so many different backgrounds and it has really given me a more worldly perspective. Not only have my interests broadened from meeting all of these people, but also my values. I hope developing a web-app for the West Medford Community center allows people to build connections with others that will allow them to gain new perspectives and new experiences.\n	\N	I have not	Malbeth the Seer	
