fic needs. ASU, who sponsors the class and projects, ran into some legal issues that shortened our time frame and cut our budget. This made us adjust our whole plan by changing our timelines and deviate from our original blueprints for the sensory boards. We had to budget things differently and look for less expensive, but still good quality, items for the boards. Overall, we met our stakeholders expectations and am really proud of my team’s communication, dedication and passion, and discipline. I really enjoyed getting to work on a project that was helping a cause I am really passionate about. 	github.com/hkniimi	7	9	3	5	6	11	2	1	4	10	8	12	I’ve done volunteer work in tutoring both in high school and here at Tufts and really enjoy it. I am very passionate about the ability to give back to my community and really enjoy working with kids! In addition, as a member of the LGBTQ+ community, I find the senior LGBTQ housing very important and something I would love to be a part of. It would be an honor to be able to give back in some way to my community. 	\N	No	Tar-Meneldur	
